# 🌍 JobGenesis - $0 Enterprise Deployment Guide

We've restructured the codebase to support a distributed, **Zero-Cost Production Deployment** using Vercel and Render. This circumvents Docker memory limitations and entirely eliminates AWS billing.

I have already injected a [render.yaml](file:///d:/project/jobGenisis%281%29/coding-gauntlet/render.yaml) (Backend Blueprint) and [vercel.json](file:///d:/project/jobGenisis%281%29/coding-gauntlet/vercel.json) (Frontend Router) directly into your repository.

### Prerequisites
1.  **Commit Your Code**: Push all the latest changes (including [render.yaml](file:///d:/project/jobGenisis%281%29/coding-gauntlet/render.yaml) and [vercel.json](file:///d:/project/jobGenisis%281%29/coding-gauntlet/vercel.json)) to your GitHub repository.
2.  **Databases**: 
    - Keep using your **MongoDB Atlas** Free Cluster.
    - Create a Free Serverless Redis database at **[Upstash](https://upstash.com/)** and copy the `REDIS_URI`.

---

## 🟢 Phase 1: Deploying the Backends (Render)
Render allows us to host the Node.js API and the Python ML Engine as two completely separate microservices for free.

1.  Create an account at **[Render.com](https://render.com/)**.
2.  Go to your Dashboard and click **New+** -> **Blueprint**.
3.  Connect your GitHub account and select your `jobgenesis` repository.
4.  Render will automatically detect the [render.yaml](file:///d:/project/jobGenisis%281%29/coding-gauntlet/render.yaml) file I created for you. It will recognize two services: `jobgenesis-api` and `jobgenesis-ml`.
5.  Click **"Apply"**.
6.  **Crucial Step**: Go to the **Environment** tab in your Render dashboard for `jobgenesis-api`. You *must* securely input the following missing values:
    *   `MONGO_URI`
    *   `JWT_SECRET`
    *   `GEMINI_API_KEY`
    *   `REDIS_URI` (from Upstash)
7.  Go to the **Environment** tab for `jobgenesis-ml` and input:
    *   `MONGO_URI`

*Note: Allow 5-10 minutes for Render to build the Node and Python environments.*

---

## 🔵 Phase 2: Deploying the Frontend (Vercel)
Vercel is the fastest, most reliable global host for React/Vite applications.

1.  Copy the URL of your new Render Node.js backend (e.g., `https://jobgenesis-api.onrender.com`).
2.  Log in to **[Vercel.com](https://vercel.com/)**.
3.  Click **Add New...** -> **Project**.
4.  Import your `jobgenesis` GitHub repository.
5.  In the "Configure Project" screen, drop down the **Environment Variables** section and add:
    *   **Name**: `VITE_BACKEND_URL`
    *   **Value**: `https://jobgenesis-api.onrender.com` *(Paste your actual Render URL here without a trailing slash).*
6.  Go back to Render, find `jobgenesis-api` -> Environment, and add your new Vercel URL as the `FRONTEND_URL` so CORS allows the connection.
7.  In Vercel, click **Deploy**.

---

### 🎉 Congratulations
Within minutes, you will have a globally distributed, microservice-based AI Recruiting Platform running completely for free. 
*   Vercel acts as your Edge CDN.
*   Render acts as your heavy-lifting computation cluster.
*   MongoDB and Upstash act as your serverless data layer. 

JobGenesis OS is now ready for world-class candidate traffic.
